    "difficulty": "Mastery",
    "difficultyReason": "Justify divisibility statements for every integer, including a product of consecutive integers."
  },
  "content": {
    "id": "p75-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "For each of these expressions, $n$ is an integer. Decide whether the statements are true or false. Explain your answer.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p75-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$5n$ is divisible by 5.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True: $5n$ is a multiple of 5.",
          "worked": "True. Since $n$ is an integer, $5n$ is a multiple of 5.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p75-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$4n+1$ is divisible by 4.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False: $4n+1$ leaves a remainder of 1 when divided by 4.",
          "worked": "False. $4n$ is a multiple of 4, so $4n+1$ leaves a remainder of 1 when divided by 4.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p75-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$4(n+1)$ is divisible by 4.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True: $n+1$ is an integer, so $4(n+1)$ is a multiple of 4.",
          "worked": "True. Since $n$ is an integer, $n+1$ is also an integer. Therefore $4(n+1)$ is a multiple of 4.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p75-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$6n$ is divisible by 2.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True: every multiple of 6 is divisible by 2.",
          "worked": "True. $6n=2(3n)$, and $3n$ is an integer, so $6n$ is divisible by 2.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p75-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$n(n+1)$ is divisible by 2.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True: one of the consecutive integers $n$ and $n+1$ is even, so their product is even.",
          "worked": "True. $n$ and $n+1$ are consecutive integers, so one of them is even. Their product therefore has a factor of 2 and is divisible by 2.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
    ]
  },
